Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["CanonicalFormSelfTest", "ObjectName",
 CellID->242645230,ExpressionUUID->"274db78f-3202-af49-9fa3-66c9936294cb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"1848e10f-04b4-4f4f-8a50-b82448b0faac"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["CanonicalFormSelfTest",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->
     "paclet:SamuelFrerichs/StructureAdaptiveEvolution/ref/\
CanonicalFormSelfTest"], 
   RowBox[{"[", "]"}]}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "be93090c-1ed9-1542-aede-6dfed0ad3cbf"],
 " \[LineSeparator]",
 "property-tests the canonical-form backends on random hypergraph states."
}], "Usage",
 CellID->327031128,ExpressionUUID->"d8b78f23-1de5-c24d-a73a-f9c4f35a69f4"],

Cell["\<\
For each universe and backend it counts invariance failures (a relabelled, \
edge-shuffled copy gets a different form), completeness failures (canonical \
equality disagrees with brute-force isomorphism on a pair of states) and \
forms that are not isomorphic copies of their input.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->646262003,ExpressionUUID->"f5220e6a-8bd5-f844-8ab7-9828ca68e4ef"],

Cell["\<\
Options: \"Universes\" ({\"Unordered\", \"Ordered\"}), \"Backends\" ({\"Exact\
\", \"Native\"}), \"Arity\" (3), \"Vertices\" (5), \"Edges\" (4), \"Trials\" \
(200) and \"RandomSeed\" (1). Zero failures on random states is evidence, not \
a proof.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->11067841,ExpressionUUID->"b1d97084-4754-da49-bc4e-54ac871b0288"]
}, Open  ]],

